# All variables are optional. With none set, Meridian runs entirely as a
# local, in-browser simulation — no signup, no keys, no blockchain required.

# --- Database (optional) ---
# Unset: uses an embedded PGLite (Postgres-in-WASM) instance, zero config.
# Set: connects to a real Postgres/Neon instance instead.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host/db

# --- AI-backed adjudication (optional) ---
# Unset: the escrow simulator falls back to a local keyword heuristic.
# Set: calls xAI's Grok API for a real LLM verdict in the simulated flow.
# XAI_API_KEY=

# --- Live GenLayer testnet mode (optional) ---
# All three below must be set together to enable the "Verify on GenLayer"
# button on a case page, which calls the REAL deployed Intelligent Contracts
# (contracts/meridian_adjudicator.py, contracts/settlement_outbox.py) on
# Testnet Bradbury. See README.md "Deploying the contracts" for how to get
# these values. GENLAYER_DEPLOYER_KEY is server-only and must never be
# committed — it signs the demo relayer's on-chain calls.
# VITE_MERIDIAN_ADJUDICATOR=0x...
# VITE_MERIDIAN_OUTBOX=0x...
# GENLAYER_DEPLOYER_KEY=0x...
